From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MDOK maintainers <maintainers@mdok.dev>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] tool: guard the parser entry point for library callers

MDOK embeds curl's command-line parser instead of invoking the curl
executable.  The upstream entry point assumes process-owned global state has
already been initialized.  Return the existing parameter error for malformed
embedding calls so the bridge can report the failure without dereferencing a
null global or operation configuration.
---
 src/tool_getparam.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/tool_getparam.c b/src/tool_getparam.c
index 35c01b1..05ac372 100644
--- a/src/tool_getparam.c
+++ b/src/tool_getparam.c
@@ -3126,7 +3126,14 @@ ParameterError parse_args(int argc, argv_item_t argv[])
   bool stillflags;
   const char *orig_opt = NULL;
   ParameterError err = PARAM_OK;
-  struct OperationConfig *config = global->first;
+  struct OperationConfig *config;
+
+  /* MDOK calls the curl tool parser as a library entry point.  Keep malformed
+     embedding calls in the normal error-return path instead of dereferencing
+     the process-global parser state. */
+  if(argc <= 0 || !argv || !global || !global->first)
+    return PARAM_BAD_USE;
+  config = global->first;
 
   stillflags = TRUE;
   for(i = 1; i < argc && !err; i++) {
-- 
